# Netlify routing.
#
# Weekly cache-bust: the SMS send includes /{week} in the URL (e.g.
# menu.havnclub.com/may10, menu.havnclub.com/welcome/may10). Each week has
# a unique URL, so messaging apps (iMessage, WhatsApp) regenerate the link
# preview instead of serving the previous week's cached image. Bump the
# prefix weekly alongside the menu deploy.
#
# Every customer menu URL serves the one index.html; pricing.js reads the
# path. The full grammar, every part optional, in this order:
#
#   /{week}/{dc|sd}/{welcome|ws|db|in}/{quiz|tasting}/via/sms/{campaign}/{kind}/{dc|sd}
#
#   week     cache-bust slug (oct04, sep27, jun7 …) so link previews refresh
#   dc|sd    city (DC is the default; SD links carry /sd)
#   mode     welcome = first order, ws = wellness credit, db = legacy ws,
#            in = win-back; none = the regular member menu
#   variant  /welcome/quiz (quiz signup), /welcome/tasting (Tasting Menu)
#   via/sms  SMS attribution suffix from HQ (intake/return_links.py). It is a
#            path, not a query string, because AT&T rotation shims drop queries.
#
# These rules MUST stay above the /:week/* asset strip below. Netlify does not
# re-evaluate a rewrite, so if /:week/* matched first it would read "welcome",
# "sd" or "via" as a week slug, rewrite /welcome/via/... to /via/... and 404.
/:week/welcome/*    /index.html  200
/:week/welcome      /index.html  200
/:week/ws/*         /index.html  200
/:week/ws           /index.html  200
/:week/db/*         /index.html  200
/:week/db           /index.html  200
/:week/in/*         /index.html  200
/:week/in           /index.html  200
/:week/sd/*         /index.html  200
/:week/sd           /index.html  200
/:week/dc/*         /index.html  200
/:week/dc           /index.html  200
/:week/via/*        /index.html  200
/welcome/*          /index.html  200
/welcome            /index.html  200
/ws/*               /index.html  200
/ws                 /index.html  200
/db/*               /index.html  200
/db                 /index.html  200
/in/*               /index.html  200
/in                 /index.html  200
/sd/*               /index.html  200
/sd                 /index.html  200
/dc/*               /index.html  200
/dc                 /index.html  200
/via/*              /index.html  200

# Strip the weekly prefix off everything else under /{week}/* — static asset
# cache-bust (e.g. /oct04/menu-preview.jpg → /menu-preview.jpg).
/:week/*    /:splat 200

# Internal weekly performance review — unguessable path, not linked from anywhere
/may10-review  /may10-review.html  200

/*          /index.html 200
